>> title: Korma
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, indian, almond, yogurt, curry
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: chicken korma, lamb korma, qorma, kurma, shahi korma, navratan korma
>> pairs-with: pilau-rice, naan, ginger-garlic-paste
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: blitz 2 min to a smooth cream
>> step.2: sweat 12 min, without letting it colour
>> step.3: fry in 2 min
>> step.4: simmer 20 min, covered
>> step.5: stir in, simmer 8 min

Blitz @blanched almonds{1/2%cup}(70 g), @raw cashews{1/4%cup}(35 g) and @hot water{3/4%cup}(180 mL) in a #blender{} ~stir{2%min}, until there is no grain left on the tongue.

Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}(finely chopped) in @ghee{4%Tbs}(56 g) in a #heavy pot{} over low heat ~fry{12%min}, with a lid on for the first half, until it is completely soft and still the colour it went in.

Fry @ginger-garlic paste{2%Tbs}(34 g), @green cardamom{6%pods}(bruised), @cloves{4}, @cinnamon{1%stick}(2-in piece) and @ground coriander{2%tsp} into @&(~1)softened onion{} ~fry{2%min}.

Simmer @boneless chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; cut in 2-in pieces), @thick yogurt{1/2%cup}(120 g; whisked smooth and stirred in off the heat) and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} in @&(~1)spiced onion{} covered ~simmer{20%min}.

Stir @&(~4)nut cream{}, @heavy cream{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @saffron{1%pinch}(soaked in a spoon of warm milk) and @rose water{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)chicken{} and ~simmer{8%min}, uncovered, until it coats a spoon.

Lamb shoulder wants an hour and goes in before the yogurt. Prawns want four minutes and go in with the cream.
